\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \relax \fontsize  {9}{10pt}\selectfont  \textbf  {EXP-AF: the decidability census, and the design rule met piecewise.} \textbf  {(1)}~crosses elicitation with items; \textbf  {(2)}~records the response channel; \textbf  {(3)}~grades a non-deception construct off that channel. \text  {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "458$}~holds; $\times $~fails; \textbf  {?}~undecidable from the release. \textbf  {Every property holds somewhere and none holds all three}, so the standard is meetable by combination rather than by invention. Corpora publishing no elicitation index and no second construct are summarized in the last row. Verdicts are gated on \emph  {admissible} item keys (DEVIATION 1); all counts are in \texttt  {eccp\_decidability.json}.}}{19}{table.caption.44}\protected@file@percent }
